# util-linux builds runuser(1) alongside su(1), so it is in the image whether or not
# anything calls it, and it needs its own PAM service for the same reason su does.
#
# runuser is root-only by design — it is su without the authentication, for a caller
# that is already root. So the auth stack is pam_rootok or nothing: uid 0 passes,
# everyone else is denied rather than prompted, because there is no password this
# program would ever check.
auth       sufficient pam_rootok.so
auth       required   pam_deny.so
account    required   pam_unix.so
session    required   pam_unix.so
